                </Data>
                <Data name="Discussion">
                    <value>1. Well East-Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands: A broad area of low pressure is forecast to form about 1000 miles east-southeast of the Hawaiian Islands over the weekend. Environmental conditions appear favorable for gradual development of this system, and a tropical depression could form late this weekend or early next week.  The system is forecast to move generally northeastward, remaining well east-southeast of the Hawaiian Islands. 
 Formation chance through 48 hours...low...20 percent. 
 Formation chance through 7 days...medium...50 percent. </value>
                </Data>
            </ExtendedData>
